1
00:04:35,555 --> 00:04:41,555
When patriots become heroes.

2
00:09:11,111 --> 00:09:17,111
Captain America: The First Avenger is a action, adventure,
science fiction film directed by Joe Johnston.

3
00:13:46,666 --> 00:13:52,666
During World War II, Steve Rogers is a sickly man from Brooklyn who's
transformed into super-soldier Captain America to aid in the war effort.

4
00:18:22,222 --> 00:18:28,222
Rogers must stop the Red Skull – Adolf Hitler's ruthless head of weaponry, and the leader of an
organization that intends to use a mysterious device of untold powers for world domination.

5
00:22:57,777 --> 00:23:03,777
Captain America / Steve Rogers, played by Chris Evans.

6
00:27:33,333 --> 00:27:39,333
Peggy Carter, played by Hayley Atwell.

7
00:32:08,888 --> 00:32:14,888
James Buchanan 'Bucky' Barnes, played by Sebastian Stan.

8
00:36:44,444 --> 00:36:50,444
Colonel Chester Phillips, played by Tommy Lee Jones.

9
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:26,000
Johann Schmidt / Red Skull, played by Hugo Weaving.

10
00:45:55,555 --> 00:46:01,555
Howard Stark, played by Dominic Cooper.

11
00:50:31,111 --> 00:50:37,111
Captain America: The First Avenger is a 2011 American superhero film
based on the Marvel Comics character Captain America.

12
00:55:06,666 --> 00:55:12,666
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Paramount Pictures, it is
the fifth film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

13
00:59:42,222 --> 00:59:48,222
The film was directed by Joe Johnston, written by Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely, and stars Chris Evans as Steve Rogers / Captain America alongside
Tommy Lee Jones, Hugo Weaving, Hayley Atwell, Sebastian Stan, Dominic Cooper, Toby Jones, Neal McDonough, Derek Luke, and Stanley Tucci.

14
01:04:17,777 --> 01:04:23,777
During World War II, Rogers, a frail man, is transformed into the super-soldier Captain America and must stop
the Red Skull (Weaving) from using the Tesseract as an energy source for world domination.

15
01:08:53,333 --> 01:08:59,333
The film began as a concept in 1997 and was scheduled for
distribution by Artisan Entertainment.

16
01:13:28,888 --> 01:13:34,888
However, a lawsuit disrupted the project and was
not settled until September 2003.

17
01:18:04,444 --> 01:18:10,444
In 2005, Marvel Studios received a loan from Merrill Lynch, and planned to
finance and release the film through Paramount Pictures.

18
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
Directors Jon Favreau and Louis Leterrier were interested in directing
the project before Johnston was approached in 2008.

19
01:27:15,555 --> 01:27:21,555
The principal characters were cast between March and June 2010.

20
01:31:51,111 --> 01:31:57,111
Production began in June, and filming took place in London,
Manchester, Caerwent, Liverpool, and Los Angeles.

21
01:36:26,666 --> 01:36:32,666
Several different techniques were used by the visual effects company Lola to create the
physical appearance of the character before he becomes Captain America.

22
01:41:02,222 --> 01:41:08,222
Captain America: The First Avenger premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on July 19,
2011, and was released in the United States on July 22, as part of Phase One of the MCU.

23
01:45:37,777 --> 01:45:43,777
The film was commercially successful, grossing over $370 million worldwide, and received positive reviews from critics,
who praised Evans' performance, the film's depiction of its 1940s time period, and Johnston's direction.

24
01:50:13,333 --> 01:50:19,333
Two direct sequels have been released: Captain America: The Winter
Soldier (2014) and Captain America: Civil War (2016).

25
01:54:48,888 --> 01:54:54,888
The film explores themes of new york city, nazi,
superhero, world war ii, heroism.

26
01:59:24,444 --> 01:59:30,444
The tone is thought_provoking.
